ok - flag on: dispatch, polled status lines, the local merge after its task's pending lines, and cleanup are recorded in order
ok - flag on: a PR merge is recorded once, after the task's pending status lines
ok - flag on: registering a PR records task.pr_ready with its full URL after the task's pending status lines, and the merge-time re-record adds nothing
ok - flag on: a worker's status command records its line at once, and the watcher backstop does not record it again
ok - flag on, state override outside the home: the worker's status command records its line at once
ok - flag on, relative config override: a worker running elsewhere still records its line at once
ok - append failing: the worker's status command exits nonzero and records nothing
ok - ledger failing: the worker's status line still lands exactly, quietly, and the backstop records it later
ok - flag off: the worker's status command is a plain append and leaves no ledger file, offset, or lock
ok - a burst past 256 lines is captured from its last 256 lines and the ledger records how many bytes it skipped
ok - a capture reads exactly the bytes it counted and leaves a late append for the next capture
ok - flag off: the whole lifecycle leaves no ledger file, offset, or lock
ok - flag on: filed, closed, and answered write exactly their fields, one line each, with ts and at the same instant
ok - closed: a repeat of the same task, evidence, and PR writes nothing; any difference writes a record
ok - closed: a replay inside one incarnation writes nothing, and the same close after a new dispatch is recorded again, for every evidence
ok - answered_by is derived from the home role and two exact source prefixes, and is unknown when neither says
ok - flag off writes nothing, and an unwritable ledger fails with one line for the producer to ignore
